{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_doc", "label": "pyinfra-provisioning: verification performed", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_highest_available_seam", "label": "\"Highest available seam\" testing philosophy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Infrastructure code's checks run through the tool's own execution engine or a real adjacent tool, not mocks -- no pytest/dry-run seam applies to a pyinfra deploy function, so the only faithful check is actually running it."}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_git_systemd_service_demo", "label": "git_systemd_service live demo (ticket 04)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Demoed against a throwaway app/unit before either real Control API Deploy file adopted it: first run applies, second run is fully idempotent (zero pending ops), a code-only change correctly triggers a restart via restarted=code_changed or unit.will_change."}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_will_change_vs_did_change", "label": ".will_change vs .did_change() distinction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "did_change() raises if read before the operation executes; .will_change is the property safe to read immediately after calling an operation during the prepare-phase diff -- confirmed by reading OperationMeta in installed pyinfra==3.9.2 and by the demo running without the RuntimeError .did_change() would raise."}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_caddyfile_validation_demo", "label": "Caddyfile.j2 validated with real caddy binary (ticket 07)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rendered templates/Caddyfile.j2 with representative values and ran caddy validate against a real stock caddy binary; wake_on_lan-dependent lines were the only ones that failed on a stock binary, confirming every directive the ticket added is genuinely valid Caddyfile syntax."}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_wake_plugin_live_validation", "label": "wake_plugin validated live, caddy-wol retired", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built a real Caddy binary with the in-repo wake_plugin module, ran caddy validate against templates/Caddyfile.j2, and ran a live caddy run smoke test against a fake Control Pi API and unreachable upstream -- matching the fail-open, throttled design in .scratch/caddy-wake-plugin/spec.md."}, {"id": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_handle_errors_bug", "label": "handle_errors-inside-handle_path bug found & fixed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/agents/pyinfra-demo.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Caddy rejects handle_errors nested inside handle_path as \"not an ordered HTTP handler\"; fixed by moving handle_errors to the site's top level, matched against orig_uri so it still only fires for /server*. Pre-existing bug, independent of caddy-wol vs call_wake_api, surfaced during ADR-0012 revalidation."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_git_systemd_service_demo", "target": "docs_agents_pyinfra_demo_highest_available_seam", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED"